this research project addresses an important gap in the literature on post-conflict economic recovery and contributes to the understanding of the long-term consequences of civil wars on developing countries' economies. the findings of this study will inform policymakers, international organizations, and donors in their efforts to support liberia's economic recovery and promote sustainable development. moreover, the project's mixed-methods approach and case study design will provide valuable insights into the complex dynamics of post-conflict economic recovery, with implications for other countries emerging from conflict.

